      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -704,
        64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 520,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## Send tagged VNTANA 3D models to Figurement for material editing\n\n### How it works\n\nTagging becomes your routing switch. When an asset is published in VNTANA, this workflow checks whether its tags include `Figurement`. If they do, it extracts the product, client, and GLB blob identifiers from the event payload, downloads the model from VNTANA, and imports it into a Figurement scene through their API, ready for material editing and review. Assets without the tag are ignored, so you control exactly which models flow downstream by adding or removing a single tag.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Install the VNTANA community node, create a VNTANA API credential, and assign it to the **Download GLB from VNTANA** node.\n- Create a Header Auth credential (name it \"Figurement API key\") with header `Authorization` and value `Bearer YOUR_FIGUREMENT_API_KEY`, and assign it to the **Import to Figurement** node.\n- Register a VNTANA webhook for asset publish events pointing at the production webhook URL.\n- Tag any asset `Figurement` and publish it to test.\n\n### Customization\n\nChange the tag name in the **Tag = Figurement?** node to route on any tag you like, point the import at a different Figurement endpoint, or add a Slack notification after a successful import."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "sticky-note-filter",
